notion:page:30d23ac1-bdd8-8050-bcdf-d66f:
{"success":true,"markdown":"Firbolg druid (Circle of the Stars)



Echo was born and raised in a small, quirky household surrounded by the greenery of a lemon grove. She grew up with a passion for nature, spending hours exploring the forest, and developing a deep connection to the earth. Her home was about 20 min away from the sea and the tides and their connection to the moon was the trigger for her to start studying stellar astronomy. At 15 she encountered her first loss, when a close friend accidentally set fire to the woods near her home. Her friend was killed and the fire burned down most of the forest and the lemon grove. As Echo struggled to come to terms with her loss, she began to experience strange and vivid dreams. These dreams always where the stars sparkling in sequence. As time progressed the line between dreams and reality blurred. Stars could "talk" to her and started to develop a deep connection with nature around her. She left home at 17 filled with a sense of adventure and purpose to discover what more the world has to offer.

Ten years later, Echo found herself in a small village on the outskirts of a dense forest, rumored to hold a mystical energy. She had heard tales of a dying forest, its water scarce and poisoned by illegal loggers. As she wandered deeper into the forest, she stumbled upon a clearing, where an eerie silence fell over her. The trees were dying, their whispers calling out to her in desperation. Echo used her connection to nature to summon a powerful storm. But in doing so, she inadvertently caused a devastating landslide that swept through the village below, destroying homes and lives. Echo was left standing amidst the wreckage, grief-stricken and heartbroken. She realized too late that her actions had caused harm, not healing. The forest's whispers fell silent, and Echo was left alone with her guilt and regret. Echo spent days wandering through the devastation, searching for answers. She sought out the villagers who had survived, trying to understand what had happened and how she could make things right. One day, Echo came face to face with the loggers who had triggered the landslide. They were ruthless and unrepentant, blaming Echo for the destruction they had help cause. Echo was torn between her anger and her desire to forgive. She chose violence. That night, the stars aligned in a way that Echo had never seen before. In her dreams (or was she awake?), she heard a clear message: "The time of reckoning has come," it said. "The balance of nature must be restored. Make amends, Echo." And so she continues to this day, learning, growing, and vowing to keep the balance","parentDb":{"id":"31a23ac1-bdd8-80f5-95e6-c03f8caef1ec","title":"Mother of Bob"},"cover":null,"icon":{"type":"file","url":"/images/notion/icon_30d23ac1-bdd8-8050-bcdf-d66f7555616e.png"}}

